The table loader, the JAX sampler, the C ABI shim and the ctypes binding were extracted from mu2e-fastsim-core
(mu2e-fastsim commit a058b04, modules cry_tables, cry_device, cry_native and native/cry/cry_shim.cc) and generalized
to be experiment-neutral; the detector projection and acceptance stayed in mu2e-fastsim.

cryjax re-implements the published CRY 1.7 model (Cosmic-ray Shower Library, Lawrence Livermore National
Laboratory, UCRL-CODE-227323). CRY is distributed under its own BSD-style licence with an additional DOE notice,
both reproduced in docs/third-party-cry.txt; they apply to CRY and to the parts of this package that reproduce it.
The CRY sources and distribution tables are not part of this repository: users obtain them from LLNL, and the
loader accepts only the release tables by SHA-256. cryjax is not produced, endorsed or supported by LLNL, the
University of California or the U.S. Department of Energy.

No experiment-internal inputs, conditions, data or physics results are part of this repository.
